**Day 2 – Understanding AI Agents**
*Objective*
Learn how AI Agents differ from a simple OpenAI workflow by introducing memory and tool usage.

 *Workflow*
Receive a chat message
Send it to an AI Agent
Use memory to retain context
Use tools when needed
Return a response
Send summary of conversation to google sheet
Book calls if requested, send the details to google sheet.
Send call details via email

*Concepts Learned*
AI Agent
LLM (OpenAI Model)
Memory
Tool Calling
Agent Orchestration

*Key Takeaway*
I learned that an AI Agent is more than just an LLM. It can reason, remember context, and use external tools to perform actions. An LLM only thinks, while an AI Agent thinks and acts. The LLM generates responses, but the agent decides when to use memory and external tools to accomplish the user's goal. 